1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,844
The pressure built for a fortnight, day by day.

2
00:00:02,844 --> 00:00:13,767
The council moved the court hearing; the industrial client added a charge for the delay; the magazine and the newspaper both asked for the same interview.

3
00:00:13,767 --> 00:00:18,377
“Go back and check the title,” the professional said.

4
00:00:18,377 --> 00:00:23,767
“If the surface is wrong, the whole file is wrong.”

5
00:00:23,767 --> 00:00:31,341
A colleague in the gallery had already written a review, and a critic in the same building had written the opposite.

6
00:00:31,341 --> 00:00:37,015
“You will gain credit with one and lose it with the other,” the accountant said.

7
00:00:37,015 --> 00:00:49,109
“That is the margin you are working in.” The manufacturer, the merchant, and the unemployed detective who shared the rack in the corridor all had an opinion.

8
00:00:49,109 --> 00:00:52,269
The fundamental problem was rent.

9
00:00:52,269 --> 00:01:01,818
The office cost more than the rice and the wash of the whole team, and the applicant with the managerial experience had already gone away.

10
00:01:01,818 --> 00:01:07,373
“Be sure of the question before you answer it,” the librarian said.

11
00:01:07,373 --> 00:01:11,512
“A gardener does not water a web.”

12
00:01:11,512 --> 00:01:20,032
The entrepreneur in the sack coat wanted a spy in the opposite team; the clerical marshal wanted lace on the cover.

13
00:01:20,032 --> 00:01:34,556
“Much of this is occupational theatre,” Lin said, “and some of it is last-minute panic.” They were already late, and the face of the client on the screen was not a friendly one.

14
00:01:34,556 --> 00:01:40,600
Together the team bought back two days by cutting a correspondent from the schedule.

15
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:44,865
“Will it be enough?” Maya asked.

16
00:01:44,865 --> 00:02:00,734
“It will be something,” he said, “and something is not nothing.” The old problem returned, as it always did: a professional must answer for the whole, not for the part they touched.

17
00:02:00,734 --> 00:02:09,738
An insider from the newspaper, a painter from the gallery, and a gardener from the roof came to the office on the last day.

18
00:02:09,738 --> 00:02:14,563
“The heart of the file is the margin,” the insider said.

19
00:02:14,563 --> 00:02:25,697
“Everything else is decoration.” A copy was available on the rack, and the man from the sack coat read it twice before he bought the magazine.

20
00:02:25,697 --> 00:02:30,252
The will to continue was there; the time was not.

21
00:02:30,252 --> 00:02:35,453
It was already quite dark outside by then.
